github.com/belluikit/goffmpeg-libs/ios_arm64
============================================

FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org) built for ios_arm64 as shared libraries, so that an app
ships them and a user can replace them (LGPL 2.1 section 6b), in two codec
sets (belluikit/goffmpeg#41). An app's binary loads one of them.

shared/ holds the media set: MP3, WAV, MP4, WebM, Ogg and HLS, with H.264,
VP9 and AV1 video and AAC and Opus audio. H.264 and AAC decode only through
Apple's VideoToolbox and AudioToolbox (h264_videotoolbox, aac_at): there is
no FFmpeg H.264 or AAC decoder here (belluikit/goffmpeg#77).

  libavcodec-goffmpeg.framework libavformat-goffmpeg.framework libavutil-goffmpeg.framework libswresample-goffmpeg.framework libswscale-goffmpeg.framework

shared-audio/ holds the audio set: MP3, WAV, Opus (in Ogg) and AAC (in MP4,
M4A and ADTS), with no libswscale and no libavdevice. AAC decodes through
Apple's AudioToolbox, aac_at (belluikit/goffmpeg#77).

  libavcodec-goffmpeg-audio.framework libavformat-goffmpeg-audio.framework libavutil-goffmpeg-audio.framework libswresample-goffmpeg-audio.framework

FFmpeg version: N-125841-ge2bc6d88cd (git revision e2bc6d88cd68184288c16570e04881c3a426a05a).
Local patches: the libraries here were built from FFmpeg with goffmpeg's
ten patches applied, patches/0001 to 0010 (BUILDING.md lists them).
Three of them change code built for iOS: 0005 and 0010 change
libavcodec/audiotoolboxdec.c, aac_at, in both libavcodecs (#77, #103), and
0006 adds libavcodec/videotoolboxdec.c, the h264_videotoolbox decoder, in
shared/'s libavcodec (#77). The other seven change FFmpeg's MediaCodec
decoders, which are not built for iOS.

